{
  "info": {
    "name": "TA Genap — Dashboard Checks (localhost)",
    "_postman_id": "b7e1a3c2-0d44-4f2a-9c11-dashboardchecks01",
    "description": "Admin dashboard endpoints (auth:sanctum + admin).\n\nAUTH: Run 'Login (admin)' first — it POSTs the seeded admin creds and saves the returned Sanctum bearer token into the {{token}} collection variable. Every other request inherits `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` from collection-level auth.\n\nSEED THE ADMIN FIRST (if not already):\n  php artisan db:seed        # creates admin123@mail.com / password123 (role=ADMIN)\nThe admin user must have role=ADMIN or the dashboard routes return 403.\n\nAlso a regression harness for two fixed OOM bugs:\n 1. Unbounded `time_frame` bucket loop in DashboardService::getAdminMetrics — see 'OOM regression'.\n 2. Sanctum guard self-recursion — any 200 here proves auth no longer recurses (token path).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "admin123@mail.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "password123", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Login (admin) → sets {{token}}",
      "request": {
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/login",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "login"]
        },
        "description": "POST /api/login with the seeded admin creds. Saves data.token → {{token}}."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "const token = b.data && b.data.token;",
              "pm.test('Got a bearer token', () => pm.expect(token, 'data.token missing').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
              "if (token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('token', token); console.log('Saved token to {{token}}'); }"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dashboard Metrics — default (7d)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "X-Requested-With", "value": "XMLHttpRequest" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "dashboard"]
        },
        "description": "GET /api/dashboard with defaults (time_frame=7 days, poll table + poll chart)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200 (not 401/403/500)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Not a 500 OOM', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.not.equal(500));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('Has metrics envelope', () => { pm.expect(b).to.have.property('success', true); pm.expect(b.data).to.have.property('chart_data'); });",
              "pm.test('chart_data is bounded (<= 5000 buckets)', () => pm.expect(b.data.chart_data.length).to.be.at.most(5000));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dashboard Metrics — 24h hourly",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "X-Requested-With", "value": "XMLHttpRequest" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard?time_frame=24h",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "dashboard"],
          "query": [{ "key": "time_frame", "value": "24h" }]
        },
        "description": "Hourly bucketing branch (time_frame ends with 'h')."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('chart_data present and bounded', () => pm.expect(b.data.chart_data.length).to.be.at.most(5000));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dashboard Metrics — vote table + vote chart",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "X-Requested-With", "value": "XMLHttpRequest" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard?time_frame=30&table_type=vote&chart_type=vote",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "dashboard"],
          "query": [
            { "key": "time_frame", "value": "30" },
            { "key": "table_type", "value": "vote" },
            { "key": "chart_type", "value": "vote" }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Exercises the vote branch of the table + chart switch."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('Has table_data + chart_data', () => { pm.expect(b.data).to.have.property('table_data'); pm.expect(b.data).to.have.property('chart_data'); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "OOM regression — huge time_frame (must NOT crash)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "X-Requested-With", "value": "XMLHttpRequest" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard?time_frame=100000000",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "dashboard"],
          "query": [{ "key": "time_frame", "value": "100000000" }]
        },
        "description": "Before the fix this allocated ~100M array entries and OOM-killed the server. The clamp (365 days) + loop cap (5000) must keep it a fast, bounded 200."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200 (no OOM 500)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Responds quickly (< 3s)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(3000));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('chart_data clamped (<= 5000)', () => pm.expect(b.data.chart_data.length).to.be.at.most(5000));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dashboard Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "X-Requested-With", "value": "XMLHttpRequest" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/health",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "dashboard", "health"]
        },
        "description": "GET /api/dashboard/health — platform health report (admin only)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200 (not 403/500)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Sanctum guard did not recurse (no 500)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.not.equal(500));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('Has health payload', () => pm.expect(b).to.have.property('success', true));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
